  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) perception of negligible probability differences and (2) preference for the lottery with the higher maximum outcome. The verbal report confirms that the individual sees the probabilities as 'almost the same', aligning with the first condition. They also explicitly favor B due to its higher winning amount, which matches the second component of the reason. Although the phrase 'ohne Risiko' is imprecise, it does not contradict the core logic of the reason. The information considered (similar probabilities, higher gain in B) and the justification (choosing B for higher gain under similar chance) closely match the structure of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
